<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Compute energy.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table A.1 ‣ Compute energy. ‣ Appendix A System Modeling Parameters ‣ LLM Inference in a Flash!" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> lists per-operation energy for CPU and SSD-CIM.
CPU operation energies are from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, assuming 7nm technology node.
Each CPU instruction incurs an additional <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sim}13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}13</annotation></semantics></math> pJ overhead from instruction fetch and register file access, estimated from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> (scaled down to 7nm using SRAM energy ratios from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>).
We assume a digital Flash CIM device as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>.
I8 MAC energy is 0.1 pJ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, and
input/output activation buffer energy is 0.8 pJ per 8 bits (extrapolated from 7nm data in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, assuming 2KB I/O buffer as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite>).
SSD-CIM SRAM overhead (<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sim}7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}7</annotation></semantics></math> pJ per 32 bits) is estimated from 1 MB SRAM read energy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>.
FP32 Div <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 6\times</annotation></semantics></math> FP32 MAC and FP32 Sqrt <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 12\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 12\times</annotation></semantics></math> FP32 MAC, estimated from Agner Fog instruction tables for Zen 7 nm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.
FP32 Exp is typically approximated using <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sim}8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}8</annotation></semantics></math> FMA instructions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, incurring <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="8\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times</annotation></semantics></math> computation and instruction overhead.</p>
</div>
